{
  "_doc": "Arena definitions. SOURCE OF TRUTH for layout: art/blender/build_map.py reads the 'brushes' of a map and authors the GLB (art/gltf/map_<id>.glb) incl. the paint-atlas UV2; the runtime reads spawns/lighting/scoring/bounds from here and geometry from the GLB. Coordinates: Y-up metres, runtime/glTF axes. SUNCREW (side A) spawns at -Z, GULF CREW (side B) at +Z. Yaw: 0 faces +Z, +90 faces +X. 'mirror': true duplicates a brush under the map's symmetry ('rot180' = (x,y,z)->(-x,y,-z), yaw+180). A map with status 'planned' has its design locked but no brushes yet — it must NOT be offered in map select until status is 'built'. A map may keep its brushes in a layout file instead: \"layout\": \"layouts/<id>.json\" (see art/blender/MAPS_README.md); spawns carry padRadius for the runtime.",
  "_changes": [
    "2026-09-28 CHANGED(CORE) ffaSpawns: cinder gained 8 FFA drop-pad spawns each (FREE-FOR-ALL, CONTRACT_FFA §F1), generated by _harness/gen_ffa_spawns.ts (farthest-point sampling over core nav nodes in rot180 mirror pairs; floor ny ≥ 0.9, ≥ 2.5 m clear of walls / edges, off grates / conveyors / springs / oob / team pads; nav distance to the centroid and to the nearest spawn within ±15 % of the mean). Authorized by the owner's FFA request; nothing else in this file changed.",
    "2026-09-28 orchestrator: cinder.ffaSpawnRules added (clear 1.8, minNy 0.85, centroidGate 0.25) and cinder.ffaSpawns regenerated with them for FFA crew balance; see the _doc inside.",
    "2026-09-30 CHANGED(WASHOUT) per-map score limits (CONTRACT_WASHOUT W1, CORE lane follow-up): every built map gained 'washout': {teamLimit, ffaLimit} (read by runtime/src/core/match/world.ts washoutLimitFor; a missing or bad value falls back to data/weapons.json washout 51 / 20). Why: the single limits reached unevenly (TEAMS 51: pier18 4/8, lockwell 8/8, cinder 0/8; FFA 20: pier18 8/8, lockwell 4/8, cinder 1/8). Tuned with npm run probe:washout:tune (node _harness/probe_bots.ts --rule washout --tune, run per map with --maps <id>): bot-only WASHOUT matches, mixed lineup, skill swell, 3:00, NO limit, seeds 1-8 per map and mode, AFTER the spawn-protection / event-order fixes of the same day (they moved the distributions: fewer fresh-spawn washes); the leader's score at the horn decides whether a limit would have been reached. Pick rule (printed by the tuner): the in-band limit whose reach is closest to 50 %, a tie going to the one nearest the median. RE-TUNED on the final core code of 2026-09-30 (after the CONTRACT_CONTROLS C2 special rule, the FFA spawn fixes — no mist rule in the unseen test, chest at feet + MOVE.skin, the regenerated pier18 / cinder ffaSites — and the held-SPECIAL fix; the first tuning of the same day gave pier18 52 / 24, lockwell 59 / 19, cinder 46 / 18, and on the final code those reached pier18 62.5 / 37.5 %, lockwell 50.0 / 25.0 %, cinder 37.5 / 12.5 %, so lockwell FFA and cinder FFA had left the band). Leaders at the horn, seeds 1-8: pier18 TEAMS 53,52,48,52,54,51,49,54 (min 48, p25 51, median 52, p75 53, max 54, mean 51.6; in band 52/53) -> teamLimit 52 = 62.5 % (5 of 8); pier18 FFA 23,22,24,22,23,21,24,26 (min 21, p25 22, median 23, p75 24, max 26, mean 23.1; in band 23/24) -> ffaLimit 23 = 62.5 % (5 of 8). lockwell TEAMS 56,61,57,61,59,58,56,61 (min 56, p25 57, median 59, p75 61, max 61, mean 58.6; in band 58/59/60/61) -> teamLimit 59 = 50.0 % (4 of 8); lockwell FFA 14,19,14,21,16,18,16,16 (min 14, p25 16, median 16, p75 18, max 21, mean 16.8; in band 17/18) -> ffaLimit 17 = 37.5 % (3 of 8). cinder TEAMS 45,43,44,47,47,43,46,45 (min 43, p25 44, median 45, p75 46, max 47, mean 45.0; in band 45/46) -> teamLimit 45 = 62.5 % (5 of 8); cinder FFA 17,15,21,16,17,16,17,16 (min 15, p25 16, median 17, p75 17, max 21, mean 16.9; in band 17) -> ffaLimit 17 = 50.0 % (4 of 8). All maps together, each match against its own map's limit: TEAMS 14 of 24 (58.3 %), FFA 12 of 24 (50.0 %). Nothing else in this file changed.",
    "2026-09-30 CHANGED(SPAWNS) ffaSites (CONTRACT_FFA_SPAWNS S1, CORE lane): pier18 24 sites (4936 m² of core floor; nearest-site nav gap min 9.0 m), lockwell 22 sites (4368 m² of core floor; nearest-site nav gap min 11.2 m), cinder 24 sites (5144 m² of core floor; nearest-site nav gap min 12.2 m) — the FFA spawn-site pool the random safe respawn draws from (runtime/src/core/match/world.ts ffaSitePool / chooseSite). Generated by node _harness/gen_ffa_spawns.ts --count auto --write: the 8 ffaSpawns (unchanged, first) + new sites under the same site rules (floor ny, clearance incl. ffaSpawnRules, off grates / conveyors / springs / oob / team pads) added in rot180 mirror pairs by hidden coverage (a seeded model of 600 layouts of 7 foes kept 14 m apart; each pair adds the most layouts with fewer than 2 available sites, an available site = no foe sees its chest (feet MOVE.skin over the floor + half the tall hit height) within 30 m and none stands within 3 m — no mist rule since the skeptic fix of 2026-09-30: canSee's mist hides only SLICK targets and a respawned runner is tall —, among the pairs keeping 9 m nav from the pool; held-out check, layouts with no available site (foes 14 / 18 m apart): pier18 3.6 / 6.2 %, lockwell 0.2 / 0.1 %, cinder 0.0 / 0.0 %); size = one site per 200 m² of core floor, even, clamped to 16-24; yaw (degrees) faces the nav path to the map centre. --check regenerates and compares. ffaSpawns kept as-is for back-compat. Nothing else in this file changed."
  ],
  "brushKinds": {
    "box": "axis-aligned solid: min, max. paintFaces: 'all' (default, never bottoms) | 'top' | 'none'",
    "ramp": "solid wedge inside min/max; its top rises from min.y to max.y toward 'rise' (+x|-x|+z|-z). The high edge meets the platform it serves.",
    "crate": "stacked-plank cargo crate; center = bottom-centre; size = edge length; yaw optional",
    "planter": "raised planter box (rim paintable, soil not); center = bottom-centre; size [w,h,d]; palm: true adds a palm (deco, trunk collides)",
    "curb": "low hazard-striped kerb; min, max",
    "spawnpad": "team spawn pad disc (NOT paintable); center = top-centre; radius; team A|B",
    "deco": "non-paintable set dressing: asset id, pos, yaw, scale, collide (bool), optional text",
    "stairs": "solid staircase inside min/max rising toward 'rise' (+x|-x|+z|-z); optional steps (default 0.25 m risers), mat, nose",
    "overlapOk": "(flag on any solid brush) true = exempt from the builder's AABB overlap warning"
  },
